# Tense TPM05.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Tense TPM05 Energy Analyser — Modbus register map for Omni Console
# | 
# | Source: TPM05_modbus_register_list_ing.pdf ("Basic Data Modbus Address").
# | - Holding registers (FC03). Addresses are the raw register addresses in
# | decimal: 4000 = 0x0FA0 … 4087 = 0x0FF7 (the manual's Dec and Hex columns are
# | the same value). `area` defaults to "holding" and is omitted below.
# | - Values are 16-bit (1 register) unless marked u32 (2 registers, Big-Endian
# | word order — `word_order` defaults to "be" and is omitted).
# | - `scale` bakes in the device's *fixed* multiplier only (×0.1, ×0.01, ×0.001).
# | 
# | CT/VT CAVEAT — voltage, current and power additionally scale by the configured
# | transformer ratios, which a static map cannot read at runtime:
# | voltage = raw × VT × 0.1     (manual: "Data * VT * 0.1")
# | current = raw × CT × 0.001   (manual: "Data * CT * 0.001")
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Tense
@model=TPM05
@description=3-phase energy analyser — V/I/P/Q/S, frequency, energy totals, power factor and THD (scaled 16/32-bit integers).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/tense-tpm05.toml; Source: TPM05_modbus_register_list_ing.pdf ("Basic Data Modbus Address").. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

